  "question": {
    "text": "Two newspapers <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> are published in a city. It is known that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of the city population reads <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> reads <math><mi>B</mi></math> while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>%</mo></math> reads both <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Further, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of those who read <math><mi>A</mi></math> but not <math><mi>B</mi></math> look into advertisements and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of those who read <math><mi>B</mi></math> but not <math><mi>A</mi></math> also look into advertisements, while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">%</mo></math> of those who read both <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> look into advertisements. Then the percentage of the population who look into advertisements is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2JWei",
      "text": "<math><mn>13.5</mn></math>",
