  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the percentage&nbsp;of population in a city who read newspaper&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Now, we know that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mover accent=\"false\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mover accent=\"false\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mover accent=\"false\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math></p><p>And,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, percentage of those who read advertisements is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>50</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1390</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Total persons who look into advertisement <math><mo>=</mo><mn>13.9</mn><mi>%</mi></math></p>",
